# Implementing a theme changer

If you haven't noticed in the `<nav>` container above, I have a `<select>` element that changes the overall style of my website.

This is easy to implement - it's basically:
- `<select>` element with `onchange` to a Javascript function
- Javascript function changes the CSS class associated with the `<body>` tag
- Other Javascript code saves the choice to `localStorage`
- On page load, pull the saved choice (if it exists), and then load that theme

To learn more, see the source code of this website.
